    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>Wait, i think i might have misread that. for APA 7th, if there are 4 authors, do i actually list them all the first time? i thought it was \"et al.\" right away for anything more than 2 or 3 people now. can you double check that for me? it's getting really messy with all these different rules.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In APA 7th, if you're citing a work with 4 or 5 authors, list all authors at first mention. After that initial citation, use \"et al.\" afterward, only if subsequent citations occur after the first mention. Be sure also that after 10 consecutive references from a single work by the same authors, you only need to include the first author's surname and the date if it's within the same year. It can get tricky, so it's a good practice to review APA's in-text citation guidelines in their full context or consult the latest APA manual for specific examples.",
