      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's quite common to feel overwhelmed by the specificities of citation styles. Consider creating a citation style check-list to have at hand as you write, where you can tick off rules as you encounter them. You could also utilize citation management software like EndNote, Zotero, or Mendeley. These tools offer robust features for managing different citation styles and can significantly reduce the manual workload and error rate. Additionally, by periodically going back through your in-text citations to ensure accuracy, you can catch inconsistencies early before the bibliography stage. Finally, practicing with citation exercises or sample papers might also aid in familiarizing yourself with the process, making it feel less arbitrary and more intuitive over time.",
